-- title:
--   Local Dedekind–Kummer criterion at a simple root
-- statement:
--   Let $P$ be an integrally closed domain with fraction field $K$, let $L$ be a field that is a finite separable extension of $K$ with $P \to L$ compatible through $K$, and let $\kappa$ be a field. Let $D$ be a $P$-subalgebra of $L$ and $\varphi \colon D \to \kappa$ a ring homomorphism such that the composite $P \to D \to \kappa$ is surjective. Let $t \in D$ be such that the $K$-subalgebra of $L$ generated by $t$ is all of $L$, and let $g \in P[T]$ be a monic polynomial with $g(t) = 0$. Assume that the image of $t$ is a simple root of the reduction of $g$, i.e. that the derivative of the image of $g$ under $P \to \kappa$ does not vanish at $\varphi(t)$. Then for every $c \in D$ whose image in $L$ is integral over $P$ and which satisfies $\varphi(c) = 0$, there exists $s \in D$ with $\varphi(s) \neq 0$ such that $s c$ lies in the ideal of $D$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak n = \ker(P \to \kappa)$ under $P \to D$.
--
--   This is the local form, at a simple root, of the Dedekind–Kummer description of the fibre of $\operatorname{Spec} D \to \operatorname{Spec} P$: after inverting an element not in $\ker\varphi$, the ideal $\ker\varphi$ of elements integral over $P$ is generated by $\mathfrak n$, so no Noetherian or Dedekind hypothesis on $P$ is needed. It is used in the study of the Igusa scheme, in the lemma [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_mul_eq_natCast_mul_add_jInvChartInf_mul_of_coeff_zero_mem`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_mul_eq_natCast_mul_add_jInvChartInf_mul_of_coeff_zero_mem).
